From 3580c36ea57051919eddd45f8bd210cff58fc7e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:15:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Agent Memory provider, with a PrecisionMemBench
 single-turn retrieval result

Agent Memory (https://github.com/MythologIQ-Labs-LLC/agent-memory) is a
governed local memory runtime: policy-checked writes to a durable SQLite
store, lexical and exact-identity candidate routes, governed admission and
ranking. No LLM at ingestion or retrieval.

The provider stores each document through the public AgentMemory.remember
API in a per-user hashed scope, and retrieve() is one
AgentMemory.recall(query, budget=k) returning the runtime's ranked prefix
unchanged. It refuses to return a fact it never ingested.

Setup:
  pip install "agent-memory-reference @ git+https://github.com/MythologIQ-Labs-LLC/agent-memory@<commit>"

Usage:
  amb run --dataset precisionmembench --split single-turn --memory agent-memory --mode retrieval

Result (unmodified harness at 03c1d0f, Agent Memory 581557f9c81f):
15/77 correct, active 4/43, mean precision 0.1806, mean recall 0.9535.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
